### What did you do?

### Playground Code
```js
const f = (function() {
    class C {
        field = this.x;
    }
}).bind(this);
```

### ESLint Configuration 
<details> 
 <summary> Tap to see full config </summary> 

```js
import { defineConfig } from "eslint/config";

export default defineConfig([
    {
        "rules": {
            "no-extra-bind": [
                "error"
            ]
        },
        "languageOptions": {
            "ecmaVersion": "latest",
            "sourceType": "module"
        }
    }
]);
```
 </details>


### What did you expect to happen?

ESLint should report `"The function binding is unnecessary."`.
The outer functions don't use `this` in their own scope — the `this` inside class fields and static blocks belongs to the class itself (instance for fields, constructor for static blocks), not the enclosing function. So `.bind(this)` on the outer function is redundant.


### What actually happened?

No problem is reported.

